  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Schlittler delivered 6.2 innings of one-run baseball while the offense broke through when it mattered most.",
    "what_this_means": "They never trailed. Got ahead in the third on three runs and held the lead through nine, converting three of ten RISP situations into actual runs instead of leaving them stranded. That's the baseline execution. Not flashy, not dominant, just clean. Ben Rice went 3-for-5 with a homer and an RBI. Jazz Chisholm Jr. went 3-for-4 with two RBIs. The pitching didn't give back what it was given. Cam Schlittler allowing one earned run over 6.2 frames against the Mets is the kind of start that wins games when the bats show up alongside it. They did, early and often enough. The bullpen. Fernando Cruz 1.1 scoreless, David Bednar 1.0 with a run. Held what mattered. This is a team that doesn't need to lead wire-to-wire to win, just needs to lead at the end. They did.",
    "what_to_watch": "Huascar Brazob\u00e1n's 2.14 ERA meets a Yankees lineup batting .236. Tonight's matchup tilts toward the pitcher's side until New York proves otherwise at Citi Field.",
